  "en": {
    "desktop": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"100%\" style=\"height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 600 310\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"nv17-diligence-en-desktop-title nv17-diligence-en-desktop-desc\" xml:lang=\"en\" data-variant=\"desktop\"><title id=\"nv17-diligence-en-desktop-title\">The due-diligence circuit</title><desc id=\"nv17-diligence-en-desktop-desc\">Due-diligence mechanism in the controls announced by BIS on 16 November 2026, section 744.24 note 3 and paragraph e. The exporter obtains and can provide sufficient information about the foreign data center’s KYC checks, including customers and their ownership or control. Refused or insufficient information creates a red flag that presumptively provides knowledge unless resolved before the transaction. Requests for documents and clarification return to the data center; no automatic clearance is shown. For a later change to a covered end use, the recipient must be informed and the operator must obtain BIS authorization under the text’s conditions.</desc><rect x=\"0.6\" y=\"0.6\" width=\"598.8\" height=\"308.8\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"var(--color-surface)\" stroke=\"var(--color-line-strong)\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"28\" font-family=\"l0g Nvidia Cloud Controls\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"var(--color-paper)\">The due-diligence circuit</text><g transform=\"translate(70 82)\" data-icon=\"racks\"><path d=\"M-22-18H-3V18H-22Z M4-18H23V18H4Z M-17-10H-8 M-17-3H-8 M-17 5H-8 M9-10H18 M9-3H18 M9 5H18 M-20 23H22\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--color-signal)\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(300 82)\" data-icon=\"lens\"><path d=\"M-13-16H3L13-6V10H-13Z M3-16V-6H13 M-7 0H4 M-7 5H1 M13 10L22 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--color-signal)\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(530 82)\" data-icon=\"document\"><path d=\"M-14-20H5L